Package: qsbsdata
Type: Package
Title: Data Sets for the Quantitative Skills in Biological Sciences (QSBS) Course
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Emiel", "van Loon", email = "e.e.vanloon@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("John", "Fieberg", role = "dtc",
           comment = "author of the Data4Ecologists package, from which 52 data sets were copied"),
    person("Ben", "Staton", role = "dtc",
           comment = "author of 'Introduction to R for Natural Resource Scientists', from which 9 data sets were copied"))
Description: A collection of data sets used in the practicals of the course
    Quantitative Skills in Biological Sciences (QSBS). Contains the data sets
    referred to in the exercises of
    chapter 8 of Dormann (2020) 'Environmental Data Analysis' (copied from
    the 'faraway', 'MASS', 'permute' and 'datasets' packages, and from the
    data archive accompanying the book), four data sets from the APES
    teaching repository (<https://github.com/biometry/APES>), and all data
    sets of the 'Data4Ecologists' package by John Fieberg
    (<https://github.com/jfieberg/Data4Ecologists>, CC0), which accompanies
    the book 'Statistics for Ecologists'. Also contains the tabular data
    sets of 'Introduction to R for Natural Resource Scientists' by Ben
    Staton (<https://bstaton1.github.io/au-r-workshop/>, CC0), used in the
    self-study module on Monte Carlo methods, with the original CSV files.
License: GPL-3
Encoding: UTF-8
LazyData: true
Depends: R (>= 3.5.0)
Suggests: MASS, tibble, dplyr
RoxygenNote: 7.3.2
